{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"AC6 corrected after plan review BLOCKED on a real contradiction I introduced. AC6 claimed a green ubuntu-latest CI leg proves the Linux bwrap write-deny; AC12 records that this repo's runners deny unprivileged user namespaces, so probe() returns None there and the enforcement tests skip silently. A green leg proves nothing about bwrap. AC6 now states the truth: Linux enforcement was measured by hand in a ubuntu:24.04 container (write outside DENIED, write inside succeeded, rm -rf <protected>/* DENIED with target surviving), and the missing gating lane is tracked as 0d22-f664-77e1-495f.\n\nFour follow-ups filed discovered_from this ticket, all from the change 2256 review advisories:\n- 724c-b5fd-efb1-40d5 (P1) _diagnose_non_killed runs surviving mutants through mutmut run WITHOUT the sandbox - the incident's exact shape, still live on main. This ticket scoped to execute_shard()'s subprocesses and never checked for mutmut run elsewhere in the module.\n- c100-c4f1-2a2b-4905 (P2) enforcement tests assert file absence with no liveness check, so they pass when the sandbox fails to launch.\n- 0d22-f664-77e1-495f (P2) no gating CI lane proves Linux bwrap enforcement.\n- baf9-eea0-4b8d-42a4 (P3) residual advisories: docs/venv contradiction, silent allow-path skip, ambient-CI fail-open, Seatbelt read/network posture."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1787856092889615001,"uuid":"ba9afae4-3a89-4866-88a5-9e6af4c1f07e"}